# Makefile.local.example — committed template for the gitignored Makefile.local.
#
# Copy to Makefile.local and fill in. Per FLEET-BUILD-DEPLOY-STANDARD
# ("Per-repo Makefile convention"), EVERY site/internal value lives here rather than in
# the committed Makefile — the universal rule, public or private, no per-repo branching.
# That keeps the internal registry hostname out of git permanently, so this repo flipping
# public later needs no scrub.
#
#     cp Makefile.local.example Makefile.local
#
# With LUX_REGISTRY unset, `make lint` / `make arch` / `make format` / `make test` skip
# cleanly with a message instead of failing on an unreachable pull — so a clean clone
# without registry access still has a working Makefile.

# The private guard registry that hosts luxarch + luxlint.
# (These images are private-registry only — they are never published to GHCR.)
LUX_REGISTRY ?= docker.<your-private-registry>
